# Embedded Systems Career Session

## Overview
Attended an expert session on building a career in Embedded Systems.

## Key Insights
- Embedded systems involve both hardware and software integration.
- Strong fundamentals in microcontrollers and C programming are essential.
- Understanding real-time systems and debugging is important.

## Skills Required
- C programming
- Microcontrollers (8051, ARM)
- Basic electronics and digital systems
- Problem-solving and debugging skills

## Career Path
- Start with basics of embedded C and microcontrollers
- Work on small projects (LED interfacing, sensors)
- Move to advanced topics like RTOS and communication protocols

## Key Takeaway
Embedded systems is a strong core field with good opportunities for those with practical skills and strong fundamentals.
